                <pb facs="0573" n="445" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg445"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 314.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to
                        Mr. Lowell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 7,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1058.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your dispatch No. 917, of
                    the 22d ultimo, in relation to Mormon recruits from India, I have to inform you
                    that Lord Granville’s suggestion as to instructing the American consuls in India
                    to co-operate with the British authorities there has been adopted by this
                    Department and that suitable instructions have been given to the consul-general
                    at Calcutta, and to our consuls at Bombay and Singapore, on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
